* PAM8302A, 2.5 W mono filterless class-D amplifier: the project's model, fitted to the
* datasheet (Diodes DS41333 Rev. 6 - 2, May 2021). Diodes publishes no SPICE model for it.
*
* Pins in the order of KiCad's symbol: SD, IN+, IN-, VDD, GND, OUT+, OUT-.
*   Input:  10k from each input pin to an internal summing node held at VDD/2 (the functional
*           block diagram, page 2; "the DC level is held at VDD/2", page 7).
*   Gain:   the differential output is 150k/10k = 15 times IN+ - IN- (A = 20*log(RF/RI),
*           page 7; the Gain row, 23.5 dB). An external RIN in series lowers it to
*           150k/(10k + RIN), as the datasheet says.
*   Speed:  the datasheet gives no bandwidth. A pole at fbw and a delay of tdel stand for the
*           modulator: 40 kHz, and 2 us, half a period of the 250 kHz oscillator (fOSC row,
*           200 to 300 kHz). The decks move both.
*   Output: each side through its switches, 0.45 ohm high side and 0.20 ohm low side (RDS(ON)
*           rows): 0.33 ohm per side on average. The swing stops at the rails.
*   SD:     the outputs run above 1.2 V on SD (VSH row) and are 0 below.
.subckt PAM8302A SD INP INN VDD GND OUTP OUTN params: fbw=40k tdel=2u
RINP INP SP 10k
RINN INN SN 10k
VSP SP MID 0
VSN SN MID 0
EMID MID GND VDD GND 0.5
HDIF D1 GND POLY(2) VSP VSN 0 150k -150k
RBW D1 D2 1k
CBW D2 GND {1/(6.283185307*1k*fbw)}
EBUF D2B GND D2 GND 1
TDL D2B GND D3 GND Z0=1k TD={tdel}
RTL D3 GND 1k
* The swing reaches the rails smoothly (tanh): a hard clamp leaves the DC solve no slope to follow.
BDIF VD GND V = u(V(SD,GND) - 1.2) * V(VDD,GND) * tanh(V(D3,GND) / V(VDD,GND))
BOP OP GND V = V(VDD,GND)/2 + V(VD,GND)/2
BON ON GND V = V(VDD,GND)/2 - V(VD,GND)/2
ROP OP OUTP 0.33
RON ON OUTN 0.33
.ends PAM8302A
